mble\n64\t\n65\tStart the file with exactly:\n66\t\n67\t```rust\n68\t//! <c file name>.c lines <A>-<B>: <short description>\n69\tuse crate::prelude::*;\n70\tuse core::ffi::{c_char, c_double, c_int, c_long, c_uint, c_ulong, c_void};\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\t`crate::prelude::*` already gives you: all libpng types\n74\t(`png_structrp`, `png_bytep`, `png_uint_32`, `png_color_16`, ...), every\n75\t`PNG_*`/`png_*` constant from png.h and pngpriv.h, `png_struct` and\n76\t`png_info` field access, the zlib bindings and constants, the\n77\t`memcpy/memset/memcmp/strlen/strcmp` shims, and **every function of\n78\tevery other translated module**. Do not re-declare anything from it.\n79\t\n80\t## 2. Function signatures\n81\t\n82\t* A C function that is **not** `static` becomes:\n83\t\n84\t  ```rust\n85\t  #[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n86\t  pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn png_foo(a: png_structrp, b: c_int) -> c_int { ... }\n87\t  ```\n88\t\n89\t  `extern \"C-unwind\"` (not `\"C\"`) — this is required everywhere so that the\n90\t  panic used internally in place of `longjmp` can propagate.\n91\t\n92\t* A C function that **is** `static` becomes a plain, but still `pub`, item\n93\t  (it must be `pub` because the C file is split over several Rust modules):\n94\t\n95\t  ```rust\n96\t  pub unsafe fn png_bar(a: png_structrp) -> c_int { ... }\n97\t  ```\n98\t\n99\t  A `static` C function used as a *callback* (i.e. its address is taken and\n100\t  stored in a `png_rw_ptr` / `png_error_ptr` / etc.) must instead be\n101\t  `pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` **without** `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`.\n102\t\n103\t* Type mapping:\n104\t\n105\t  | C | Rust |\n106\t  |---|---|\n107\t  | `png_structp`, `png_structrp` | `png_structrp` (`*mut png_struct`) |\n108\t  | `png_const_structp`, `png_const_structrp` | `png_const_structrp` (`*const png_struct`) |\n109\t  | `png_infop`, `png_inforp` | `png_inforp` (`*mut png_info`) |\n110\t  | `png_const_infop/rp` | `png_const_inforp` |\n111\t  | `int` | `c_int` |\n112\t  | `unsigned int` | `c_uint` |\n113\t  | `long` | `c_long` |\n114\t  | `double` | `c_double` (or `f64`) |\n115\t  | `float` | `f32` |\n116\t  | `size_t`, `png_alloc_size_t` | `usize` |\n117\t  | `ptrdiff_t` | `isize` |\n118\t  | `char*` / `png_charp` | `png_charp` (`*mut c_char`) |\n119\t  | `const char*` / `png_const_charp` | `png_const_charp` |\n120\t  | `void*` / `png_voidp` | `png_voidp` |\n121\t  | `png_uint_32` | `png_uint_32` (`u32`) |\n122\t  | `png_byte` | `png_byte` (`u8`) |\n123\t  | `uInt` (zlib) | `uInt` (`c_uint`) |\n124\t  | `uLong` (zlib) | `uLong` (`c_ulong`) |\n125\t  | `FILE *` | `*mut c_void` |\n126\t  | `char out[29]` param | `*mut c_char` |\n127\t  | `png_warning_parameters p` param | `*mut [c_char; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_SIZE]` |\n128\t  | function pointer typedefs | the `Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn ...>` aliases in the prelude |\n129\t\n130\t* Functions marked `PNG_NORETURN` (`png_error`, `png_chunk_error`,\n131\t  `png_longjmp`, `png_fixed_error`, `png_safe_error`) already have return\n132\t  type `!` in this crate. So `png_error(pp, msg);` diverges — code after it\n133\t  is dead, exactly as in C. Don't add `return`s that C doesn't have; if the\n134\t  compiler complains about unreachable code the crate has\n135\t  `#![allow(unreachable_code)]`.\n136\t\n137\t## 3. Body translation\n138\t\n139\t* Wrap nothing: the whole `fn` is already `unsafe`, so use raw pointer\n140\t  dereferences directly. `png_ptr->width` → `(*png_ptr).width`.\n141\t* `foo->bar` → `(*foo).bar`; `a[i]` on a pointer → `*a.add(i)`.\n142\t* **Pointer arithmetic**: `p + n` → `p.add(n)`, `p - n` → `p.sub(n)`,\n143\t  `++p` → `p = p.add(1)`, `*p++ = v` → `*p = v; p = p.add(1)`,\n144\t  `*--p = v` → `p = p.sub(1); *p = v`.\n145\t  If an index can be negative use `p.offset(i as isize)`.\n146\t  Taking the address of a struct field: `&png_ptr->background` →\n147\t  `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*png_ptr).background)` (or `&mut (*p).f` when a\n148\t  reference is fine).\n149\t* **C integers wrap and never panic.** The release profile has\n150\t  `overflow-checks = false`, but be defensive in obviously-wrapping code:\n151\t  use `wrapping_add/sub/mul/neg`, and for `x - y` on unsigned values that\n152\t  the C code allows to go negative use `wrapping_sub`.\n153\t  Never use `as` casts that could panic — `as` never panics in Rust, so\n154\t  plain `as` is the right translation of every C cast.\n155\t  Float → int C casts truncate: `x as i32` in Rust also truncates. OK.\n156\t  For `(png_byte)x` use `x as png_byte`; for `(int)(char)x` use\n157\t  `x as i8 as c_int`.\n158\t* **Right shifts** of signed values are arithmetic in both languages: OK.\n159\t  Shifts by >= bit width are UB in C; write the same expression, it will\n160\t  not be reached.\n161\t* **Division by a variable** which C guarantees non-zero: write it plainly.\n162\t* `sizeof x` → `core::mem::size_of_val(&x)`;\n163\t  `sizeof (T)` → `core::mem::size_of::<T>()`;\n164\t  `sizeof arr` for `T arr[N]` → `N * size_of::<T>()` (usually just `N` for\n165\t  `char`/`png_byte` arrays — read the C carefully).\n166\t* `memcpy(d, s, n)` → `memcpy(d as *mut u8, s as *const u8, n)`.\n167\t  `memset(d, v, n)` → `memset(d as *mut u8, v as u8, n)`.\n168\t  `memcmp(a, b, n)` → `memcmp(a as *const u8, b as *const u8, n)`.\n169\t  (Use `memmove` if the C used `memmove`.)\n170\t* **String literals**: `\"foo\"` as a `png_const_charp` argument →\n171\t  `c\"foo\".as_ptr()`. A C string literal split over lines with implicit\n172\t  concatenation must be joined into one `c\"...\"`.\n173\t  A `static const char x[] = \"abc\";` becomes\n174\t  `pub static x: [c_char; 4] = [b'a' as c_char, ...];` — or, more simply,\n175\t  `pub const x: &[u8] = b\"abc\\0\";` and use `x.as_ptr() as *const c_char`.\n176\t  Prefer whichever keeps the code readable; the bytes must match.\n177\t* **Local arrays**: `char buf[32];` → `let mut buf: [c_char; 32] = [0; 32];`\n178\t  then `buf.as_mut_ptr()` where C used `buf`.\n179\t  `png_byte buf[4];` → `let mut buf: [png_byte; 4] = [0; 4];`.\n180\t  C leaves them uninitialised; zeroing is safe and behaviourally identical\n181\t  for this code base (it always writes before reading).\n182\t* **`static` file-scope C variables** → `pub static NAME: [T; N] = [...]`\n183\t  (immutable) — keep the C name.\n184\t* **Structs declared locally in the C file**: the shared ones\n185\t  (`png_image_read_control`, `png_image_write_control`,\n186\t  `compression_state`) are already in `crate::shared` (in the prelude) —\n187\t  use them, do not redefine. Any other local `typedef struct` that only\n188\t  your range uses, define at the top of your file with `#[repr(C)]`.\n189\t* **`for (;;)` / `goto`**: use `loop {}` + `break`/`continue` with labels.\n190\t  A forward `goto err;` is best modelled by a labelled block:\n191\t  ```rust\n192\t  'err: {\n193\t      ...\n194\t      if cond { break 'err; }\n195\t      ...\n196\t      return x;\n197\t  }\n198\t  /* err: */\n199\t  ...\n200\t  ```\n201\t  Keep the control flow *identical*.\n202\t* **`switch`**: use `match` with `_ =>` for `default`. C fall-through must be\n203\t  reproduced explicitly (duplicate the code or restructure with `if`).\n204\t  Beware: several libpng constants have the *same value*\n205\t  (`PNG_NUMBER_FORMAT_u == PNG_NUMBER_FORMAT_d == 1`); if two match arms\n206\t  would collide, use an `if/else if` chain instead.\n207\t* **Comma expressions / assignment-in-condition**: hoist into statements,\n208\t  preserving evaluation order exactly.\n209\t* `png_debug*(...)` → delete (they are no-ops in this build).\n210\t* `PNG_UNUSED(x)` → delete (or `let _ = x;`).\n211\t* `png_voidcast(T, v)` / `png_constcast(T, v)` / `png_aligncast(T, v)` →\n212\t  `v as T`.\n213\t* `png_float(pp, fixed, s)` → `png_float_of(fixed)` (prelude).\n214\t* `png_fixed(pp, fp, s)` / `png_fixed_ITU(...)` are real functions here\n215\t  (the macro form is disabled) — just call them.\n216\t* `PNG_ROWBYTES(pd, w)` → `PNG_ROWBYTES(pd as u32, w as png_uint_32)`.\n217\t* `png_composite(c, fg, alpha, bg)` → `c = png_composite(fg as u16, alpha as u16, bg as u16)`\n218\t  (note: it *returns* the value here instead of assigning through a macro\n219\t  argument); likewise `png_composite_16(c, fg, alpha, bg)` →\n220\t  `c = png_composite_16(fg as u32, alpha as u32, bg as u32)`.\n221\t* `png_has_chunk(pp, cHNK)` → `png_file_has_chunk!` does not exist; write\n222\t  `((*png_ptr).chunks & png_chunk_flag_from_index(PNG_INDEX_cHNK)) != 0`.\n223\t  `png_file_add_chunk(pp, i)` → `(*png_ptr).chunks |= png_chunk_flag_from_index(i);`\n224\t* `PNG_STRING_FROM_CHUNK(s, c)`, `PNG_CSTRING_FROM_CHUNK(s, c)`,\n225\t  `PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING(s)` are `unsafe fn`s in the prelude taking\n226\t  `*mut png_byte` / `*const png_byte`.\n227\t* `png_handle_result_code` values are the `c_int` constants\n228\t  `handled_error`, `handled_discarded`, `handled_saved`, `handled_ok`;\n229\t  functions returning that enum return `c_int`.\n230\t* Math from `<math.h>`: `floor(x)` → `x.floor()`, `pow(a,b)` → `a.powf(b)`,\n231\t  `log(x)` → `x.ln()`, `log10(x)` → `x.log10()`, `exp(x)` → `x.exp()`,\n232\t  `ceil(x)` → `x.ceil()`, `fabs(x)` → `x.abs()`,\n233\t  `frexp(v, &e)` → use the helper `png_frexp(v)` returning `(f64, c_int)`\n234\t  which you may define locally if you need it (mimic C exactly:\n235\t  `m in [0.5,1)`, `v == m * 2^e`, and `frexp(0) == (0, 0)`),\n236\t  `modf(v, &i)` → `let i = v.trunc(); let frac = v - i;`.\n237\t  `abs(i)` on `c_int` → `i.abs()` (use `wrapping_abs` if `i` may be\n238\t  `INT_MIN`).\n239\t  `DBL_MIN`/`DBL_MAX`/`DBL_DIG` → `f64::MIN_POSITIVE` / `f64::MAX` / `15`.\n240\t* zlib: `deflateInit2(&pp->zstream, l, m, w, mem, s)` →\n241\t  `deflateInit2(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, l, m, w, mem, s)`;\n242\t  `inflateInit2(&pp->zstream, w)` → `inflateInit2(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, w)`.\n243\t  `PNGZ_MSG_CAST(s)` → `s` (as `*const c_char`); assigning a literal to\n244\t  `zstream.msg` is `(*png_ptr).zstream.msg =