{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LB5ZNXL837BXaiCiCNGZdu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# libpng → Rust translation conventions (READ FULLY BEFORE WRITING CODE)\n2\t\n3\tYou are translating **one contiguous line range of one C file** from\n4\t`../c_src/src/` into **one Rust module file** in `src/`.\n5\tThe crate is a `cdylib` that must export the *exact* public ABI of the C\n6\tlibrary and produce **byte-identical** output. Treat this as a\n7\t**mechanical, line-by-line transliteration**. Do NOT redesign, do NOT\n8\t\"improve\", do NOT fix bugs, do NOT reorder checks, do NOT change messages.\n9\t\n10\t## 0. Ground rules\n11\t\n12\t* Never modify anything under `c_src/`.\n13\t* Only write the single `src/<your-module>.rs` file you are assigned.\n14\t  Do not touch `lib.rs`, `types.rs`, `pngstruct.rs`, `pngpriv.rs`,\n15\t  `shared.rs`, `zlib.rs`, `cabi.rs`, or any other module.\n16\t* Translate **every** function in your assigned range, in the same order.\n17\t* Keep the original C comments (they document subtle behaviour).\n18\t* Keep C identifier names verbatim (`png_do_expand`, `iout`, `dp`, ...).\n19\t* The build config is `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h`. **Every** `#ifdef`\n20\t  in that file that is `#define`d is ON. In particular ON:\n21\t  READ, WRITE, SEQUENTIAL_READ, PROGRESSIVE_READ, SETJMP, STDIO,\n22\t  CONSOLE_IO, USER_MEM, USER_LIMITS, SET_USER_LIMITS, BENIGN_ERRORS,\n23\t  BENIGN_READ_ERRORS, WARNINGS, ERROR_TEXT, FLOATING_POINT,\n24\t  FLOATING_ARITHMETIC, FIXED_POINT, ALIGNED_MEMORY, POINTER_INDEXING,\n25\t  READ/WRITE_TRANSFORMS, all chunk types incl. cICP/cLLI/mDCV/eXIf,\n26\t  SIMPLIFIED_READ/WRITE (+BGR/AFIRST/STDIO), MNG_FEATURES,\n27\t  READ_COMPOSITE_NODIV, 16BIT, EASY_ACCESS, INCH_CONVERSIONS, IO_STATE,\n28\t  INFO_IMAGE, TEXT, TIME_RFC1123, CONVERT_tIME, COLORSPACE, GAMMA,\n29\t  SET_OPTION, HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN, STORE/SAVE/SET/READ/WRITE_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS,\n30\t  USER_CHUNKS, READ_USER_CHUNKS, CHECK