ing`, `png_safecat`, `png_format_number`, `png_set_error_fn`, `png_internal_longjmp` (pngerror.rs); `png_malloc_warn`, `png_malloc_base`, `png_free`, `png_set_mem_fn` (pngmem.rs); `crc32`, `inflateReset`, `Z_*`, `voidpf`, `uInt`, `uLong` (zlib); `crate::cabi::free`; `memcmp`/`memset`; `PNG_CSTRING_FROM_CHUNK`, `PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY`, `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN`, `PNG_USER_*` limits, `PNG_NUMBER_FORMAT_*` (pngpriv.rs); `PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING`, `PNG_LIBPNG_VER`, `PNG_FREE_*`, `PNG_INFO_*`, `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_AS_DEFAULT`, `jmp_buf` (types.rs).\n\n**Notes on non-obvious translation choices:**\n- Top-of-file `PNG_CHUNK` compile-time assertions skipped as instructed.\n- `png_zalloc`/`png_zfree` use plain `extern \"C\"` with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` so their types match `zlib::alloc_func`/`free_func`.\n- `png_create_png_struct` uses `catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(...))` in place of `setjmp`, with `longjmp_fn = Some(png_internal_longjmp)` and `jmp_buf_ptr` pointing at a local `jmp_buf`; `*png_ptr = create_struct` became `copy_nonoverlapping` (a memcpy, as in C). Raw pointers `cs`/`cjb` to the locals are used inside the closure to avoid Rust borrow restrictions while keeping semantics identical.\n- `PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING[i]` in `png_user_version_check` is read via raw-pointer arithmetic rather than slice indexing so it cannot panic (the C loop provably stops at i==3).\n- The `APPEND_STRING`/`APPEND_NUMBER`/`APPEND` macros in `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` are expanded inline; `PNG_FORMAT_NUMBER(number_buf, ...)` expanded to `png_format_number(buf, buf+5, ...)` since `sizeof number_buf == 5`.\n- `png_zstream_error` uses a `match` with the `default:`/`case Z_OK:` fall-through folded into the `_` arm (all zlib codes plus `PNG_UNEXPECTED_ZLIB_RETURN = -7` are distinct, so no pattern collision).","usage":{"total_tokens":129424,"tool_uses":26,"duration_ms":304140},"uuid":"7c8b3f55-2634-42d9-ae52-6042ba253076","session_id":"bedb3620-db7f-4287-b934-614ec17ac76e"}
