n[1][0] B_MASKS(1,1) = 0x0f0f0f0f, 0x33333333, 0x55555555\n[1][1] B_MASKS(2,1) = 0xff00ff00, 0x0f0f0f0f, 0x33333333\n[1][2] B_MASKS(4,1) = 0xffff0000, 0xff00ff00, 0x0f0f0f0f\n```\nValues were not hand-derived: I compiled the verbatim C preprocessor macros (`PNG_LSR/PNG_LSL/S_COPY/B_COPY/PIXEL_MASK/MASK_EXPAND/S_MASK/B_MASK/S_MASKS/B_MASKS`) with gcc and printed the resulting arrays, so they are byte-identical to the C build. The `MASK(pass,depth,display,png)` macro (including `DEPTH_INDEX`) is reproduced as a local closure; the macro definitions themselves are preserved as comments.\n\n## Notes on config-dependent branches\n\n- `PNG_USE_COMPILE_TIME_MASKS` = 1 → compile-time-mask branch translated; the runtime `#else` alternative was skipped.\n- `PNG_ALIGN_TYPE` resolves to `PNG_ALIGN_SIZE` (3) ≠ `PNG_ALIGN_NONE`, so the `default:` case's 32-bit and 16-bit aligned-copy paths **are** compiled and were translated in full. `png_isaligned(ptr, T)` was expanded inline exactly as the macro does — including the truncating cast of the address to `T` before masking (`(ptr as usize as png_uint_16) & 1`, `(ptr as usize as png_uint_32) & 3`).\n- `PNG_READ_PACKSWAP_SUPPORTED` and `PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED` are ON: all three PACKSWAP branches in `png_do_read_interlace` (bit depths 1, 2, 4) plus the `end_mask` PACKSWAP branch in `png_combine_row` are translated; the `#ifndef PNG_READ_PACKSWAP_SUPPORTED PNG_UNUSED(transformations)` tail was dropped.\n- The `switch (bytes_to_copy)` in `png_combine_row` has cases 1/2/3/default with no fall-through (every arm returns or loops forever); the `switch (row_info->pixel_depth)` in `png_do_read_interlace` has cases 1/2/4/default. There is no `default: png_error(...)` in this range — the only `png_error` in the interlaced path is `\"invalid user transform pixel depth\"` when `pixel_depth & 7`. The other three are `\"internal row logic error\"`, `\"internal row size calculation error\"`, `\"internal row width error\"`.\n- Interlace helpers used from the prelude: `png_pass_start_col`, `png_pass_col_offset`, `png_pass_inc`. `png_pass_start`/`ystart`/`yinc` were not needed by this range.\n- Pointer decrements that can legitimately step one element before `row` at the end of the expansion loops (`dp--`, `sp--`, `dp -= pixel_bytes`) use `wrapping_sub` rather than `sub`; identical codegen, avoids UB-flagged out-of-bounds `offset`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1491,"cache_read_input_tokens":94946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1491,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018wqynw38KuR3qPrhdR6c7s","session_id":"bedb3620-db7f-4287-b934-614ec17ac76e","uuid":"bfe0fa14-d764-4f19-9a58-70291d6b02f6","timestamp":"2026-08-31T12:43:53.095Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pngrutil.c 3227-3953"}
