eff`, `gamma_table`, `gamma_from_1`, `gamma_to_1`, `gamma_16_table`, `gamma_16_from_1`, `gamma_16_to_1`, `gamma_shift`. **No calls to functions in other modules**, hence no unresolved-symbol errors from this file.\n\n**Notes / deviations worth flagging:**\n- The task brief said `png_do_unshift` uses a local `png_uint_16 shift[4]`; the actual C source (line 2403) declares `int shift[4]`. I followed the source and used `[c_int; 4]`, since the values are `bit_depth - sig_bits->x` and can legitimately go negative before the `<= 0` clamp — a `u16` array would change behaviour.\n- The brief also mentioned `PNG_DIV65535`/`PNG_DIV257` and `png_gamma_16bit_correct`/`png_gamma_8bit_correct`; none of those appear anywhere in lines 2293–3333, so none are used. `png_do_rgb_to_gray`'s `PNG_READ_GAMMA_SUPPORTED` branches (8-bit `gamma_to_1`/`gamma_from_1`/`gamma_table`, and 16-bit `gamma_16_to_1`/`gamma_16_from_1`/`gamma_16_table` with `gamma_shift` indexing) are all reproduced, including both `#else` fallbacks.\n- Preserved the apparent C bug in `png_do_unpack` case 4: `shift = 4` (not `shift += 4`) in the else branch.\n- Pointer arithmetic uses `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub` rather than `add`/`sub`. Several of these loops legitimately walk one element before the start of `row` (e.g. `png_do_unpack`'s `dp`/`sp`, `png_do_gray_to_rgb`'s `dp`/`sp`), and `png_do_unpack`'s `row_width - 1` underflows when `row_width == 0`; `wrapping_*` is arithmetically identical to C while avoiding Rust's out-of-bounds-`offset` UB.\n- All `png_byte`→`int` promotions before shifts/subtracts/`|` are made explicit via `as c_int` (e.g. `(255 - (*sp as c_int)) as png_byte`, `((hi as c_int) << 8) | (lo as c_int)`), and the `rc*red + gc*green + bc*blue` sums are done in `png_uint_32` as C's usual arithmetic conversions require."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":90561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_