scale_16` test; the `#ifdef __GNUC__ default:` arm is active (gcc build) and emits `\"bad data option (internal error)\"`.\n- `__COVERITY__` branches are inactive, so `back_alpha = output_encoding == P_LINEAR ? 65535 : 255` and `output_encoding == P_LINEAR ? 65535U : 255U` are used.\n- `cmap_entries`, `output_processing`, `data_encoding`, `background_index`, `step/i/val/trans/back_alpha` kept as `c_uint`; `back_r/g/b` as `png_uint_32`; `PNG_CMAP_*` / `P_*` constants cast to `c_uint` at comparison sites to reproduce C's usual-arithmetic-conversions exactly.\n- Postfix `i++` inside `png_create_colormap_entry(display, i++, ...)` is split so the *old* value is passed and the increment happens before the call — same observable arguments as C, since the callee cannot see `i`.\n- `PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_SIZE`/`_CHANNELS`/`_COMPONENT_SIZE` are not in the prelude, so I added three private `#[inline] fn img_*_read` helpers at the top of the file (same precedent as `pngwrite_b.rs`); only `PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_SIZE` is actually used, for the `memcmp` colour-map entry comparison at C 2605.\n- `PNG_PASS_*` macros mapped to the prelude fns `png_pass_cols`, `png_pass_start_col`, `png_pass_col_offset`, `png_pass_start_row`, `png_pass_row_offset`; the `continue` on an empty ADAM7 pass increments `pass` first, matching the C `for` loop.\n- `first_row + y * row_step` uses `first_row.offset((y as isize) * row_step)`; the negative-`row_step` adjustment in `png_image_read_colormapped` uses `((*image).height.wrapping_sub(1) as isize) * (-row_step)`.\n- All 13 error message strings reproduced byte-for-byte (`\"gray[8] color-map: too few entries\"`, `\"ga-alpha color-map: too few entries\"`, `\"color map overflow (BAD internal error)\"`, etc.), in the original order.\n\n## External identifiers referenced\n\nFrom `pngread_b.rs` (peer): `png_create_colormap_entry`, `png_colormap_compose`, `make_gray_colormap`, `make_gray_file_colormap`, `make_ga_colormap`, `make_rgb_colormap`, `png_image_skip_unused_chunks`.\nFrom `pngread_a.rs`/`pngread_d.rs`: `png_gamma_not_sRGB`, `png_read_row`, `png_read_update_info`.\nFrom `pngrtran_*`/`pngtrans`: `png_set_packing`, `png_set_interlace_handling`, `png_set_background_fixed`, `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed`, `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed`, `png_set_scale_16`, `png_set_tRNS_to_alpha`, `png_resolve_file_gamma`, `png_gamma_16bit_correct`.\nOther: `png_error`, `png_malloc`, `png_free`, `png_safe_execute`, `png_get_rowbytes`, `memcmp`, `png_sRGB_table`, `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR`, `PNG_DIV51`, `PNG_DIV257`, `PNG_RGB_INDEX`, and the `P_*` / `PNG_CMAP_*` / `PNG_*_COLORMAP_ENTRIES` constants from the prelude (none redefined).","usage":{"total_tokens":131903,"tool_uses":30,"duration_ms":505907},"uuid":"4c2a7daf-28a9-4a63-9ef1-052c4fa80cb4","session_id":"bedb3620-db7f-4287-b934-614ec17ac76e"}
