ly divergences ever seen were libpng's own reads of *uninitialised* padding bits beyond the image width in `png_read_png`-allocated rows — proved to be non-determinism in the reference library itself (the C build differs from **itself** across two runs with a perturbed heap: 439 hunks). With byte-aligned widths both builds are bit-identical and run-to-run deterministic.\n\n## Design notes\n- 27 modules mirroring the C files (`png_a..d`, `pngrutil_a..e`, `pngrtran_a..e`, `pngread_a..d`, `pngset_a/b`, `pngwrite_a/b`, `pngwutil_a..c`, plus `pngerror`, `pngmem`, `pngget`, `pngtrans`, `pngwtran`, `pngpread`, `pngrio`, `pngwio`) — ~33 k lines, a near-mechanical raw-pointer transliteration preserving every message string, check order and arithmetic width.\n- Links the system zlib (`build.rs`: `-lz`) so DEFLATE output is bit-identical to the reference build.\n- `png_struct`/`png_info`/`png_control` are `#[repr(C)]` with field order matching `pngstruct.h`/`pnginfo.h`.\n- All exports use `extern \"C-unwind\"` (ABI-identical to `\"C\"`), which lets the three internal `setjmp`/`longjmp` sites (`png_create_png_struct`, `png_free_jmpbuf`, `png_safe_execute`) be implemented with `catch_unwind`; the application-facing `png_jmpbuf`/`png_longjmp_fn` path still calls the app's real `longjmp`.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (the CMake build dir I used for the reference `.so` has been removed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":595828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":217,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bedb3620-db7f-4287-b934-614ec17ac76e","uuid":"0a4d3b75-d295-4b06-b0af-49d3f2168f53","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:06:22.510Z"}
